    "note": "Signed Act 06/03/2024. Gun parts are a small part of a larger protection-order procedure act. Section 6 amends 13-14-105.5(1) only to add the capitalised words 'TEMPORARY OR PERMANENT' before 'civil protection order'; the rest of the sentence is lower-case words in a section the bill amends and may be struck, so it is not quoted (check the page image). Section 7 (13-14-106) repeats the firearm and ammunition notice for the temporary order; its printed text is garbled by strike-through, so it is not quoted."
  },
  "operative_text": "Section 4 (C.R.S. 13-14-104.5): IF THE TEMPORARY PROTECTION ORDER IS BASED IN WHOLE OR IN PART ON AN ACT OF DOMESTIC VIOLENCE, AS DEFINED IN SECTION 18-6-800.3, AND THE ACT OF DOMESTIC VIOLENCE INVOLVED THE THREAT OF USE OF PHYSICAL FORCE, USE OF PHYSICAL FORCE, OR ATTEMPTED USE OF PHYSICAL FORCE, THE CITATION MUST ALSO INFORM THE RESPONDENT THAT THE RESPONDENT MUST COMPLY WITH SECTION 13-14-105.5 BY REFRAINING FROM POSSESSING OR PURCHASING ANY FIREARM OR AMMUNITION FOR THE DURATION OF THE ORDER AND RELINQUISHING FOR THE DURATION OF THE ORDER ANY FIREARM OR AMMUNITION IN THE RESPONDENT'S IMMEDIATE POSSESSION OR CONTROL OR SUBJECT TO THE RESPONDENT'S IMMEDIATE POSSESSION OR CONTROL.\nSection 6 (C.R.S. 13-14-105.5(1)): TEMPORARY OR PERMANENT"
}